move, edit, delete, archive, unlock and needs all take `ID[,ID,...]`. `karr show 1,2` answers

    Task 1,2 not found on this board:
      karr list --compact

which is a lie about the board, and `karr show 1 2` is "unexpected extra argument". An agent that wants three cards in full runs show three times or reaches for `list --json` and filters.

## What to build

`show ID[,ID,...]` printing the cards one after another: JSON an array (as list does), text separated by a blank line, compact one line each. `--me/--last/--agent` remain exclusive with positional ids. If show is meant to stay single instead, the answer is a usage error (exit 2) whose last line is the working command; prefer the batch, the plumbing exists. Changes entry, tests.

Pointers: Role::BoardAccess/parse_ids is the shared ID[,ID,...] splitter the batch commands use; Cmd::Show takes one positional today. Cmd::Needs is the read-mostly command that already takes the list form, compare it. One id not found inside a batch: report it, still print the others, exit 1, the batch rule of ADR 0002.

